// Local-only build-setting secrets. Currently unused: the Telegram feedback
// feature that used to read TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN/TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID from here
// (via Info.plist $(VAR) substitution) now reads a plain Swift constant
// instead — see HoursTracker/Config/LocalSecrets.swift — because that
// mechanism doesn't depend on Xcode's build-setting/Info.plist substitution
// pipeline cooperating.
//
// Kept around as working xcconfig -> project.yml -> Info.plist plumbing for
// any *future* secret that's genuinely easier to inject as a build setting
// (e.g. something read by a build phase script rather than by app code).
// This file is committed with EMPTY values on purpose — the repo is public,
// so a real secret must never be typed in here and pushed. If you do add one:
//   1. Fill in its value below.
//   2. Run this once so git stops tracking further edits to this file:
//        git update-index --skip-worktree HoursTracker/Config/Secrets.xcconfig
//   3. Add it to project.yml's Info.plist properties (or wherever it's consumed)
//      and re-run `xcodegen generate`.
